# demo-video fake-agent cassette — Claude Code TUI (Phase A sample)
#
# Format: <delayMs>|@input <TAB> <payload>
#   - payload is expanded with `printf %b` (\e, \n, \t, \\)
#   - `{{INPUT}}` is replaced with the line CommandMate sent into the pane
#   - `@input` blocks until CommandMate's send arrives; numeric rows sleep first
#
# Provenance: the escape sequences reproduce real `tmux capture-pane` frames of a
# Claude Code session, taken from tests/unit/skills/orchestrate-monitor/fixtures/
# live-idle.json and live-generating-token.json (captured live, sanitized). The
# anchors the product actually keys on are preserved verbatim:
#   running -> "esc to interrupt" (CLAUDE_INTERRUPT_HINT_PATTERN) and the
#              spinner+U+2026 line (CLAUDE_THINKING_PATTERN)
#   ready   -> a line starting with U+276F (CLAUDE_PROMPT_PATTERN) plus a
#              200-char U+2500 separator (CLAUDE_SEPARATOR_PATTERN)
# Stripping the ANSI or shortening the separator breaks real detection, so do not
# "tidy" this file. See SKILL.md > fixture の採取手順 to record a fresh one.
